From 5cae4f0867009dfc5fecd5e7c6b783f93db182d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:45:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 334/395] Unified: "Motion to Video" - an assembly moving, as a
 video

The engine's animation could only be made by a script drawing each crank
angle. A revolute joint picked offers "Video" on the bar: it is turned
from one angle to another in steps ("Turn to an angle" for the time of
the video), each step is taken from the 3D view as it is seen (direction,
section, colours; the joints' markers hidden), and the pictures become an
MP4 with ffmpeg (H.264), else an animated GIF. Angles where the joints do
not hold are said. MotionVideo.export(joint, out, ...) does the same
without the screen with Part's renderImage, in one frame for all the
pictures (the box the parts sweep).

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestMotionVideo

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
